          {
            "end": 1086,
            "passage_index": 1,
            "quote": "FFAR4 acts as the selective receptor for the omega-3 fatty acid docosahexaenoic acid (DHA). It activates two divergent signaling pathways. The Galphaq-dependent cascade facilitates intracellular calcium mobilization and ERK1/2 activation. Meanwhile, beta-arrestin-2 recruitment inhibits NF-kappaB. These collective actions reshape the cytokine environment. In macrophages, DHA-FFAR4 signaling lowers the levels of TNF-alpha, interleukin-6 (IL-6), and IL-1beta while increasing IL-10 secretion.",
